    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 222,
        "text": "Hi everyone, thanks for coming to this short tour. I’m Maya, and I coordinate the public programs here at the Northside Library. Today I want to show you how we make expert knowledge accessible to ordinary residents.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "9ba0a7b01025c2c2b18055d9ae828a0bff030b54faea230e6131b4bb6180e0be",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 232,
        "sourceEnd": 311,
        "text": "Sorry to interrupt—did you say “expert knowledge”? What does that mean exactly?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "53118f3644ccb42aa3f3e76ec6f0fe8f263910b76b7f549740805d38f587d843",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 319,
        "sourceEnd": 607,
        "text": "Good question. It means we invite specialists—doctors, engineers, lawyers—to explain their work in simple language. We don’t expect people to have university degrees. Last year we ran forty-two workshops, and more than six hundred people attended. That’s twice as many as the year before.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "1efbb1b609195927340873b1660e78fed3aaf2e7b38b44f6b709884e60fe6f48",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 617,
        "sourceEnd": 654,
        "text": "Wow. So who pays for these workshops?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "ceef92080bf7534a51a50003c4a867f6d88bd3ec0364b192dfeb45adc35359a2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 662,
        "sourceEnd": 883,
        "text": "The city gives us a small grant, but most of the money comes from volunteers. We have about thirty regular volunteers, and they help with everything from setting up chairs to translating handouts into Chinese and Spanish.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "d0c182369ba50cdde7d64d62529eeda3e05cc4815dba1fa2c7d2dec0a5f61d96",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 892,
        "sourceEnd": 1058,
        "text": "I’m Priya, by the way. I’m a nurse, and I came to one of your health talks last month. I found it really useful. But I noticed the room was quite full—maybe too full?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "95a56933aa62d3eaf63578477ad593020ab8c3e0b1bdf4656ab744e270e303ed",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1066,
        "sourceEnd": 1313,
        "text": "You’re right. The health talk was the most popular event we’ve ever had. We had to turn away almost fifty people because the room only holds eighty. So next month we’re moving the big talks to the community hall, which seats two hundred and fifty.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "cfa6c477dbb7a4cd92e5ebb8f8fdd24036ac8fc8d20bff7d43bf2c3f6c7e6389",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1322,
        "sourceEnd": 1388,
        "text": "That’s a big improvement. Will you still keep the small workshops?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3558531deb81025b39fd6e197e664f1d058d07964efb27d77611aca1dcaa6476",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1396,
        "sourceEnd": 1643,
        "text": "Yes, definitely. The small ones are for hands-on practice—for example, a session on how to read a medical report. Those work best with fewer than twenty people. The large talks are more like lectures, with a question-and-answer session at the end.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "7da6174bfa8f87e6ed2f01f49d5a54af49cc8e5431c6b3a06270b87e440edda2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1653,
        "sourceEnd": 1716,
        "text": "Do you record the talks? I sometimes can’t come in the evening.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "d028e1050b153e0c438a6686062215303d118ea4354ae87b75e8999106d7eaa0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1724,
        "sourceEnd": 1961,
        "text": "We do now. Since January we’ve posted every talk online, and each video has been watched at least three hundred times. Some have been watched more than a thousand times. The online audience is actually larger than the in-person audience.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "08bca8ad5b2d1eb8df1bf564acab68ab72b47150d30f4b70695d286a168113cb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1970,
        "sourceEnd": 2028,
        "text": "That’s interesting. But not everyone has internet at home.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "c526743a49d28975d0830e2c3382d650203c7a89cce7bfd5745c9f3be357e31d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2036,
        "sourceEnd": 2248,
        "text": "Exactly. That’s why we also keep printed summaries at the front desk. They’re free, and they’re written in plain English. We print five hundred copies of each summary, and they usually disappear within two weeks.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "b893b349c75909d239bb0302c4a6d4ebc9aa78710c0dcd9da20d62f2f4e42568",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2258,
        "sourceEnd": 2317,
        "text": "So the library is becoming more like a community classroom?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "11c0f96a8bf5dda6b38ab898657180fb09c608562db8e067646e40f19db14ca5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2325,
        "sourceEnd": 2486,
        "text": "That’s a nice way to put it. Our goal is simple: fewer barriers, more access. Anyone with a library card can join—no fees, no tests, no prior knowledge required.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "e8e141c2eb1aeeb7c24751ed02f2f52e724f7b375ceecea72e88549d7b5423a6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 2495,
        "sourceEnd": 2541,
        "text": "I’ll definitely tell my colleagues about this.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "d71cead1a0f02dc07b865d65be526f722bca33d3b06e37833f4912667a66bf76",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2549,
        "sourceEnd": 2715,
        "text": "Please do. And if either of you wants to volunteer, we always need more help. The next training session is on the first Saturday of next month, at ten in the morning.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "5e3e6ea4cd8851e594815448fb565d6180409f8c693f9b2660e0c16dec578086",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
